
                                                   COMP COMMAND


Lists the infoblocks whose compatibility must be set or tested.

Below is the syntax :
                                  comp 	-addr blkAddress  -depaddr depBlkAddress 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -addr       |    Start address of the infoblock that is compatible with next block.
   -depaddr    |    Start address of the next compatibility dependent infoblock.
   -fc         |    "set" triggers the update of compatibility based on dependency link provided by "comp" command.
               |    "test" tests the already set compatibility. Mandatory switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in medc18.hex
	blklink -start 0x0060C100 -next 0x00610100
	blklink -start 0x00610100 -next 0x0
	writecks -fc set	
	comp -addr 0x00610100 -depaddr 0x0060C100 -fc set
	write -out output.hex -lyt 0x20
	
